load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A polytope: a shape with flat sides, the higher-dimensional generalization of a polygon and a polyhedron, the convex
# hull of finitely many points. The regular polytopes are the perfectly symmetric ones, and in four dimensions there is
# a unique self-dual one, the 24-cell, with twenty-four vertices, which is the seed of the whole substrate. The form
# carries the ambient vector space and the vertex count; the regularity and the face structure are developed in the
# 24-cell file, where the dimension and symmetry counts are machine-checked.
form polytope
  link space, like vector-space
  link vertices, like natural
